# CQ 27: How do the qualities of service of a case differ from each other?
#
# Where a case carries more than one communication, the question is what each
# promises against the others. A model of a plant reaches this question as soon
# as one path is time critical and another is not.
#
# Reported per parameter rather than per communication, so the comparison reads
# down a column: one row per parameter, with the communications stating it and
# the values they state.
#
# The single communication cases answer with one entry per parameter, which is
# the degenerate case of the same question and still worth returning: it says
# what the one communication promises.
PREFIX iso7498: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498#>
SELECT ?parameter
       (COUNT(DISTINCT ?communication) AS ?statedBy)
       (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT CONCAT(STR(?quantity), " ", STR(?unit)); separator=" | ") AS ?values)
WHERE {
  ?communication iso7498:hasQualityOfService/iso7498:hasValue ?v .
  ?v iso7498:forParameter ?p ; iso7498:quantity ?quantity ; iso7498:unit ?unit .
  BIND(REPLACE(STR(?p), ".*#", "") AS ?parameter)
} GROUP BY ?parameter ORDER BY ?parameter
